requirements:
To prevent UV chalking and degradation, surface coatings must conform to specified chemistries based on grade:
a) Polyester (PE): Allowed for Grade 2;
b) Super Durable Polyester (SDP): Allowed for Grades 2, 3, 4, 5, and 2S;
c) Polyvinylidene Fluoride (PVDF): Allowed for Grades 1, 2, 2S, 3, 4, and 5;
d) Fluoroethylene Vinyl Ether (FEVE): Allowed for Grades 1, 2S, 3, 4, and 5.
